    ],
    "text": "Financial Assistance from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) for the Second Integrated Road",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.039999961853027,
      11.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      224.93,
      284.2,
      408.91,
      296.91
    ],
    "text": "Investment Program (i Road 2)- Tranche 5",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow,Bold",
      "Malithi Web",
      "Times New Roman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      11.039999961853027
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      108.02,
      310.66,
      526.12,
      393.17
    ],
    "text": "The Government of Sri Lanka has successfully concluded discussions with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to mobilize a loan amounting to USD 90 million under the Second Integrated Road Investment Program (iRoad 2) \u2013 Tranche 5. The objective of this program is to enhance road transport efficiency by improving connectivity between selected rural communities and key socioeconomic centers, while also strengthening the institutional capacity of national road agencies.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow",
      "Arial Narrow,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      108.02,
      407.14,
      526.05,
      484.27
    ],
    "text": "The loan, extended from ADB will support the upgrading of approximately 500 kilometers of rural access roads to all-weather, climate-resilient standards that are inclusive and friendly to the elderly, women, children, and persons with disabilities. In addition, the program will facilitate the rehabilitation of about 21 kilometers of national roads, and the maintenance of 100 kilometers of rural access roads.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow",
      "Arial Narrow,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      108.02,
      500.4,
      526.16,
      545.83
    ],
    "text": "The Ministry of Transport, Highways and Urban Development serves as the Executing Agency, while the Road Development Authority (RDA) functions as the Implementing Agency for the program.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      108.02,
      561.84,
      526.12,
      638.95
    ],
    "text": "The Loan Agreement was formally signed on 31 October 2025 at the General Treasury, Colombo, between the Government of Sri Lanka and the Asian Development Bank. Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma, Secretary, Ministry of Finance, Planning and Economic Development, signed on behalf of the Government of Sri Lanka, while Mr. Takafumi Kadono, Country Director, ADB Sri Lanka Resident Mission, signed on behalf of the Asian Development Bank.",
    "fonts": [
      "Arial Narrow"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      108.02,
      655.11,
      362.93,
      732.8
    ],
